        "id": 1157738
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-31T01:45:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So, if old_content !\u003d content that means make_writable() could not use the original buffer (content) and had to recreate a new one. An example of that would be if a read-only file mmap\u0027ed directly was to be rewrapped as writable. We can\u0027t directly take those pages representing read-only file and wrap them as writable, so we would have to reallocate a new set of pages which do not contain the same data as the original one. And since this is a newly allocated buffer (new content) we do not need to clear it. Does that make sense?",
      "parentUuid": "1b7bf037_ec224f12",
      "revId": "34f3d36c2737f67ba0ecd3fe3f0dc619f9c23aee",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
